# @NAME@ — Gamebuino AKA CORE v1.4

ESP32-S3 at 240 MHz, 8 MiB flash, octal PSRAM, 320×240 display on an
8-bit i80 bus, four-bit SDMMC card and TAS2505 audio codec. Wiring is based
on the official jmp42/Gamebuino_AKA_lib, not the earlier assumed SPI panel.

Build and flash: `pio run -t upload`. The application partition is 0x370000
bytes. RGB565 rows are doubled horizontally and scaled vertically to 240
lines. Saves and states use the FAT16/FAT32 card. Cartridge RAM stays in
RAM; battery saves are written to the card.

D-pad or joystick, A, B; RUN or D is Start, MENU or C opens options (hold
half a second). L1/R1 are currently unused. Return to launcher currently
restarts the chip: there is no verified AKA launcher handoff protocol.

The build also emits firmware.sym from its exact ELF for gm0.
The ELF can run in gm0's experimental AKA machine. Timing there is estimated.
Hardware checks (panel colours/orientation, audio, SD, joystick) remain
necessary; a successful build is not device validation.
